WEBVTT

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.610
Storm's coming.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.520
And you boys, you are
smack in the middle of it.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:25.240
Dad wants us to pick up where he left
off... saving people, hunting things.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:28.220
Family business.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.220
I'm gonna save as many people as we can.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.900
Dean, you and I have seen things
most people couldn't even dream about.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:38.920
If it's supernatural, we kill it.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.010
End of story. That's our job.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.460
No, Dean, that is not our job.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.860
Our job is hunting evil.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.320
They're all the same, Sam.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.860
They're not human, okay?

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.730
We have to exterminate
every last one of them.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.450
Our lives are weird, man.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.410
You're telling me.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.760
We're lost.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.370
No.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:16.750
This is a short cut...

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.860
Babe, it's just we've been on this road over
an hour, and we haven't seen a single car.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.240
Molly, I know how to
read a frickin' map, okay?

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.160
We passed a gas station a while back.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.080
Let's just go ask someone.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:28.940
That was 40 minutes ago.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.080
We're not turning around.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.730
Come on.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:34.460
Isn't this argument a little archaic?

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.970
Men can ask directions these days.

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:37.790
No, we can't.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.030
It's against our genetic code.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.930
Look, I know exactly where we are.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.490
Oh, yeah? Where?

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.380
Highway 99, okay?

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.980
It cuts right through.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.110
Highway 99, huh?

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:59.810
Okay, so we're taking the scenic route.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.480
David.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.890
It's our anniversary, and we're
spending it stuck in the car.

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:05.970
I know.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.230
I'm sorry.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.670
Let me make it up to
you, okay? Come here.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.960
Stop. I'm mad at you.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.780
Oh, come on, Molly.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.210
Hey, you love me.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.450
No, I don't.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.070
You're a jerk.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:24.090
David, I mean it.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.150
Molly!

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.400
David?

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.640
David?

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.490
David?

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:30.970
David?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.850
Da... David?!

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.110
David?!

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.910
David?

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.730
Hello?

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.830
Is anyone here?

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:31.180
Hello?

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.860
It's you.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.330
You're okay.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:53.520
I'm so sorry.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.930
I didn't see you there.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.540
Are you...

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:58.270
Are you hurt?

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:00.910
Sir?

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:43.150
Stop!

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.350
You've got to help me.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.180
Please.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.150
Please!

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:55.800
All right, all right.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.250
Calm down, calm down.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.490
Tell us what happened.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.890
I-I swerved,
a-And we crashed.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:06.060
And when I came to, the car was
wrecked and my husband was missing.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:11.060
I went looking for him, but that's when the
man from the road, he... he started chasing me.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.170
Did he look like he lost
a fight with a lawn mower?

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.230
How did you know that?

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.760
Lucky guess.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:23.070
Ma'am, what's your name?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.180
Molly.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.000
Molly Mcnamara.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.160
I think maybe you should come with us.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.080
We'll take you back into town.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.280
I can't.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.430
I have to find David.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.790
He might have gone back to the car.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:34.410
We should get you somewhere safe first.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.830
Then Dean and I will come back.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:36.770
We'll look for your husband.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:37.230
No.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.390
I'm not leaving here without him.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.870
Would you just take me
back to my car, please?

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.190
Of course.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:50.530
Come on.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.610
It's right over there.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:19.820
I don't understand.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.060
I'm sure this is where it was.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.980
W-We hit that tree right there.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:27.140
This... this doesn't make any sense.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.180
Dean, we got to get out of here.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.820
Greeley could show up at any second.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:34.630
What are you gonna tell her.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.730
The truth?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.630
She's gonna take off running
in the other direction.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:43.120
I know it sounds crazy, but
I crashed into that tree.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.500
I don't know who could've taken it.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.200
It was totaled.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:50.220
Please. You have to believe me.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.390
Molly, listen, we do believe you.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.520
But that's why we want
to get you out of here.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.240
What about David?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.450
Something must have happened.

00:07:58.450 --> 00:07:59.690
I have to get to the cops.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.150
Cops... that's a great idea.

00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.920
We'll take you down to
the station ourselves.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.130
So just come with us.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.690
It's the best way we can
help you and your husband.

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:12.810
Okay.

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.200
We're supposed to be in lake Tahoe.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.930
You and David?

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.260
It's our five-Year anniversary.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:30.580
Hell of an anniversary.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.960
Right before, we were
having the dumbest fight.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.580
It was the only time we ever really
argued... when we were stuck in the car.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.840
Yeah.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.810
I know how that goes.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.380
You know the last thing I said to him?

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.640
I called him a jerk.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:51.630
Oh, god.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:56.080
What if that's the last
thing I said to him?

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.240
Molly...

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:01.130
We're gonna figure out what
happened to your husband.

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:02.620
I promise.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.520
Did you? No.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:16.440
I was afraid you'd say that.

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:20.550
This song.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.200
What?

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.400
It was playing when we crashed.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.510
She's mine.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.240
She's mine.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:36.960
She's mine.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:38.530
What is that?

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:44.390
Hold on.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.560
What are you doing?

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.120
What the...

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.980
What the hell just happened?

00:09:58.980 --> 00:09:59.570
Don't worry, Molly.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.120
Everything's gonna be all right.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:06.370
Spoke a little too soon, Sammy.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.750
I don't think he's gonna let her leave.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:40.140
This can't be happening.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.350
Well...

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.510
Trust me, it's happening.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.680
Well...

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:58.900
Okay.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.870
Thanks for helping, but I think
I got it covered from here.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:02.830
Wait.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:03.730
Molly, Molly, wait a minute.

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:04.780
Just leave me alone.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:05.980
No. Please. You have to listen to me.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.040
Just stay away.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.500
It wasn't a coincidence
that we found you, all right?

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.190
What are you talking about?

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.340
We weren't cruising for chicks
when we ran into you, sister.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.580
We were already out here.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:16.750
Hunting.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:18.660
Hunting for what?

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:21.590
Ghosts.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:25.850
D... d... don't...

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.760
Sugar coat it for her.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:29.060
You're nuts.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.220
Really?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:33.510
About as nuts as a vanishing
guy with his guts spilling out.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.380
You know what you saw.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.680
We think his name is Jonah Greeley.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:53.440
He was a local farmer that died
15 years ago on this highway.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:55.720
Just stop.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:12:00.460
One night a year, on the anniversary
of his death, he haunts this road.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.150
That's why we're here, Molly.

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.490
To try and stop him.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:11.230
Now, I suppose this ghost
made my car disappear, too.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.800
Crazier things have happened.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:13.840
Huh?

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:15.570
You know what?

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.910
I'm all filled up on crazy.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.810
I'm gonna get the cops myself.

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:22.340
I don't mean to be harsh, but I
don't think you're gonna get too far.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.630
What is that supposed to mean?

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.890
Means that plan "a" was
trying to get you out of here.

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:30.470
Obviously that didn't go over too
well with, uh, farmer road kill.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.880
Molly, we're telling the truth.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.870
Greeley's not gonna let
you leave this highway.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:46.260
You're s... you're serious
about this, aren't you?

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.120
Deadly.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.370
Everyear, Greeley finds someone
to punish for what happened to him.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.270
Tonight that person is you.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:00.070
Why me?

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.790
I didn't do anything.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.040
Doesn't matter.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:06.590
Some spirits only see what they want.

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:14.560
So you're saying this
Greeley, he took my husband?

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:18.470
Oh, god.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.810
Molly, look, we're
gonna help, all right?

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:25.690
But first, you got to help us.

00:13:26.940 --> 00:13:28.100
Help you?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.670
How?

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:35.910
This is it.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.390
This is where I saw him.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.250
Must have been his hunting cabin.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.440
Seemed like a real sweet guy.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.360
No markers or headstones outside.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.010
You're looking for Greeley's grave?

00:13:59.010 --> 00:13:59.980
Yeah.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.150
Why?

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:03.520
So we can dig up the
corpse and salt and burn it.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.270
Oh.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:07.140
Sure. Naturally.

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.990
It's a way to get rid of a spirit.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:10.920
And that'll save David?

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:14.420
This is what'll help both of you,
provided there's a corpse to be found.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:16.700
So how do we find it?

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:17.740
Uh, not sure.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:19.890
After Greeley died, his
wife claimed the body.

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.660
And that was the last anyone saw of her.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.070
So good guess she brought him back here.

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:24.880
But they have a thousand acres.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:26.910
He could be buried anywhere on 'em.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.660
Is is really what you guys do.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:30.180
You're like ghost busters.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:30.730
Yeah.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:31.810
Minus the jumpsuits.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:33.840
This is a fascinating
conversation and all.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:37.140
But this highway is only haunted once a year,
and we got till sun up to wrap this thing up.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.880
What do you say we move it along, okay?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:40.510
Great.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:52.670
What are we looking for?

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.040
Greeley's house.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.630
Maybe he's buried there.

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.480
Look for roads or paths or something.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.530
Stay close.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:14:59.010
Yeah.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:15:00.380
Okay.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:08.320
Molly?

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:11.190
Molly, help me.

00:15:12.190 --> 00:15:13.440
Molly?

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:20.090
David? David?

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:28.580
Whoops.

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.360
Hey!

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.310
Are you all right?

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:38.110
What has that son of a
bit chdone with my husband?

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:40.720
Just take it easy, all right?

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:42.050
You're gonna see David again.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:42.840
You will.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:44.060
Hey.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.960
Follow the creepy brick road.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.610
Go ahead.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.860
That thing shoots rock salt?

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:06.300
Yep.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.880
And plain salt keeps away spirits?

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:11.470
Simple remedies are always the best.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:16.710
In most cultures, salt is a symbol of purity,
so it repels impure and unnatural things.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:18.890
Same reason you throw
it over your shoulder.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:27.190
You know, just once I'd like to
round the corner and see a nice house.

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:03.980
Any headstones outside?

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:04.780
Yeah, right.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.160
Is it ever that easy?

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.910
I guess not.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.180
You two check upstairs.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.580
See if you can find any notes or
records telling us where he's buried.

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:22.860
I'll just check down here.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:51.670
Great.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.260
Look at this.

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:24.110
It's Greeley and his wife.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.840
It's a love letter he wrote her.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:49.510
My god, it's beautiful.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:57.860
I don't understand how a guy like
this can turn into that monster.

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.300
Spirits like Greeley are,uh...

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:07.140
Like wounded animals.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:09.480
Lost.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:13.760
In so much pain, that they lash out.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:14.810
Why?

00:19:14.810 --> 00:19:16.090
Why are they here?

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:18.570
Well, there's some part of them that...

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:20.880
That's keeping them here.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:24.420
Like their remains or, um...

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.280
Unfinished business.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.410
Unfinished business?

00:19:31.970 --> 00:19:32.700
Yeah.

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:35.850
It could be revenge.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.780
Could be love.

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:39.160
Or hate.

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:43.630
Whatever it is, they
just hold on too tight.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:46.460
Can't let go.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:48.170
So they're trapped.

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.990
Caught in the same loops.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:56.450
Replaying the same
tragedies over and over.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.760
You sound almost sorry for them.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:01.400
Well, they weren't
evil people, you know?

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:03.640
A lot of them were good.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:05.020
Just...

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:07.490
Something happened to them.

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:10.620
Something they couldn't control.

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:15.650
Sammy's always getting a little J. Love
Hewitt when it comes to things like this.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.940
Me, I don't like 'em.

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.190
And I sure as hell ain't
making apologies for 'em.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:26.650
There's nothing downstairs.

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:32.320
Uh, just about every piece of
mail or receipt they ever had.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.760
Looked through a couple, but
nothing about a grave so far.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:40.870
What?

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.350
There's something behind here.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.240
Here.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:01.380
It's locked from the inside.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.190
Smells like old lady in here.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:38.660
And that would explain why.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.230
Well, now we know why
nobody ever saw her again.

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.120
She didn't want to live without him.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:56.160
Dean, give me a hand.

00:21:58.660 --> 00:21:59.520
Really?

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.500
What are you gonna do?

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:07.720
We can't leave her like this.

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:08.840
Why not?

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.980
She deserves to be put to rest, Dean.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:23.330
So...

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:31.210
So, if you manage to put
Greeley to rest, too...

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:33.920
What happens to them?

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:38.100
Lady, that answer is
way beyond our pay grade.

00:22:38.300 --> 00:22:40.920
You hunt these things, but you
don't know what happens to them?

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:42.440
Well, they never come back.

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:43.910
That's all that matters.

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:49.810
After they let go of
whatever'skeeping them here, they...

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:51.970
They just go.

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:55.580
I hope someplace better,
but we don't know.

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:58.390
No one does.

00:22:58.460 --> 00:23:00.310
What happens when you burn their bones?

00:23:01.180 --> 00:23:06.530
Well, my dad used to say that was
like death for ghosts, you know?

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:07.950
But...

00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:10.280
The truth is, we still don't know.

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:12.420
Not for sure.

00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:19.280
Guess that's why we all
hold on to life so hard.

00:23:20.820 --> 00:23:22.050
Even the dead.

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:25.570
We're all just scared of the unknown.

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:28.750
The only thing I'm
scared of is losing David.

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:32.600
I have to see him again.

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:45.840
I have to.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:14.300
I think we should tell
her about her husband.

00:24:14.470 --> 00:24:15.360
We can't.

00:24:17.610 --> 00:24:20.990
Dean, it's cruel, letting
her pine for him like this.

00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:22.470
I don't like keeping her in the dark.

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:23.730
It's for her own good.

00:24:29.680 --> 00:24:32.440
I know you feel guilty,
butlet's just stick to the plan.

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:33.430
Let's get her out of here.

00:24:33.430 --> 00:24:34.280
Then we'll tell her.

00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:35.440
Tell me what?

00:24:37.870 --> 00:24:39.570
What aren't you telling me?

00:24:42.890 --> 00:24:43.600
It's about David.

00:24:43.600 --> 00:24:45.260
You know what happened to him.

00:24:45.800 --> 00:24:47.240
Molly Sam, don't.

00:24:47.260 --> 00:24:48.400
Don't what?

00:24:49.590 --> 00:24:52.210
Don't tell me because
I'll mess up your hunt?

00:24:52.270 --> 00:24:55.040
You don't care about me or my husband.

00:24:55.040 --> 00:24:56.370
That's not true.

00:24:56.370 --> 00:24:57.440
Really?

00:24:59.130 --> 00:25:01.490
Then whatever it is, tell me, please.

00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:11.280
He's coming.

00:25:13.040 --> 00:25:14.000
Stay with her...

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.280
He's got Molly!

00:26:48.950 --> 00:26:50.220
This guy is persistent.

00:26:50.410 --> 00:26:51.450
We got to find Molly.

00:26:51.600 --> 00:26:52.930
We got to find Greeley's bones.

00:26:52.930 --> 00:26:57.550
And, uh, no pressure or anything, but we
got less than two hours before sunrise.

00:26:59.040 --> 00:26:59.940
Hey.

00:27:01.100 --> 00:27:02.010
What do you got?

00:27:03.730 --> 00:27:05.710
"February 6, 1992. "

00:27:06.230 --> 00:27:08.040
That was like two weeks
before the accident, wasn't it?

00:27:08.040 --> 00:27:08.860
Yeah.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.810
It looks like the hunting cabin, but...

00:27:11.360 --> 00:27:14.440
I swear there's a tree there
right where they're standing.

00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:19.340
Should have thought of it.

00:27:19.340 --> 00:27:20.450
What?

00:27:20.450 --> 00:27:21.830
It's an old country custom, Dean.

00:27:21.830 --> 00:27:23.970
Planting a tree as a grave marker.

00:27:25.650 --> 00:27:28.580
You're like a walking
encyclopedia of weirdness.

00:27:30.920 --> 00:27:31.630
Yeah.

00:27:31.630 --> 00:27:32.780
I know.

00:27:34.560 --> 00:27:35.770
Where's David?

00:27:36.800 --> 00:27:37.980
What did you do to him?

00:27:39.830 --> 00:27:42.190
You shouldn't worry about him anymore.

00:27:43.060 --> 00:27:44.320
Oh, my god.

00:27:44.490 --> 00:27:46.860
You should worry about yourself.

00:27:47.880 --> 00:27:49.420
I didn't do anything to you.

00:27:49.560 --> 00:27:50.640
Oh?

00:27:53.740 --> 00:27:55.990
I know... I know about your wife.

00:27:56.760 --> 00:27:58.830
Hurting me won't bring her back.

00:28:00.770 --> 00:28:02.370
My wife is gone.

00:28:05.560 --> 00:28:09.330
All I got left'shurting you.

00:28:17.770 --> 00:28:19.790
P-Please.

00:28:19.790 --> 00:28:21.430
Just let me go.

00:28:21.600 --> 00:28:22.610
Go?

00:28:24.130 --> 00:28:25.300
You're not gonna leave.

00:28:26.220 --> 00:28:28.590
You're never gonna leave.

00:28:39.360 --> 00:28:40.450
Go get Molly.

00:28:53.730 --> 00:28:54.710
Oh, thank god.

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:56.700
Call me Dean.

00:29:04.660 --> 00:29:06.200
This guy's really pissing me off.

00:30:26.160 --> 00:30:28.040
Oh, baby, it's been a long night.

00:30:33.630 --> 00:30:34.360
All right.

00:30:36.500 --> 00:30:37.980
Let's get you out of here.

00:30:38.690 --> 00:30:42.750
I'm not going anywhere until you
tell me what happened to my husband.

00:30:44.010 --> 00:30:44.850
Molly...

00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:49.330
All this time I've been looking
for him, and you knew that...

00:30:50.430 --> 00:30:52.330
You knew that Greeley
killed him, didn't you?

00:30:55.620 --> 00:30:56.500
He's dead.

00:30:58.200 --> 00:30:59.250
No, Molly.

00:31:00.930 --> 00:31:02.520
David's alive.

00:31:02.950 --> 00:31:03.690
What?

00:31:05.470 --> 00:31:06.510
You're sure?

00:31:07.740 --> 00:31:08.840
I'm sure.

00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:11.650
We'll take you to him.

00:31:11.650 --> 00:31:12.870
Come on.

00:31:33.160 --> 00:31:35.260
He's in that house right there.

00:31:37.300 --> 00:31:38.380
I don't understand.

00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:40.820
You will.

00:32:00.750 --> 00:32:02.690
That's not...

00:32:07.240 --> 00:32:08.360
It can't be.

00:32:17.570 --> 00:32:18.930
What's happening?

00:32:21.740 --> 00:32:22.770
Who is that?

00:32:25.070 --> 00:32:26.530
That's David's wife.

00:32:34.580 --> 00:32:36.060
I'm sorry, Molly.

00:32:38.310 --> 00:32:42.640
15 years ago, you and your husband
it Jonah Greeley with your car.

00:32:46.480 --> 00:32:48.000
What are you saying?

00:32:48.880 --> 00:32:51.940
We're saying there isn't just
one spirit haunting highway 41.

00:32:51.940 --> 00:32:53.250
There are two.

00:32:54.050 --> 00:32:56.110
Jonah Greeley and you.

00:32:56.550 --> 00:33:00.820
For the past 15 years, one night a year
you've been appearing on that highway.

00:33:00.820 --> 00:33:02.570
No. That's not possible.

00:33:03.320 --> 00:33:06.330
It was our anniversary...
February 22nd...

00:33:06.330 --> 00:33:07.830
1992.

00:33:07.830 --> 00:33:08.890
Yes.

00:33:08.890 --> 00:33:11.360
Molly, it's 2007.

00:33:15.910 --> 00:33:17.240
Oh, god.

00:33:17.390 --> 00:33:19.090
All right. Tell me about highway 41.

00:33:19.090 --> 00:33:21.240
12 accidents over 15 years.

00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:24.150
Five of them fatal, all of them
happening on the same night.

00:33:24.150 --> 00:33:26.100
So what are we looking
at... interstate dead zone?

00:33:26.100 --> 00:33:27.310
Phantom hitchhiker? What?

00:33:27.310 --> 00:33:28.250
Not quite.

00:33:28.600 --> 00:33:31.420
Year after year, witnesses said
the same thing made 'em crash

00:33:31.420 --> 00:33:36.800
A woman appearing in the middle of the
road being chased by a man covered in blood.

00:33:36.800 --> 00:33:38.100
Two spooks?

00:33:52.650 --> 00:33:54.170
Now, where is Molly buried?

00:33:54.600 --> 00:33:57.170
She... she wasn't buried anywhere.

00:33:57.990 --> 00:33:59.330
She was cremated.

00:34:01.820 --> 00:34:03.640
So much for burning her bones.

00:34:03.690 --> 00:34:05.570
Yeah, but then what's keeping her here?

00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:17.490
Some spirits only see what they want.

00:34:18.590 --> 00:34:19.950
David?!

00:34:20.420 --> 00:34:21.450
David?

00:34:22.410 --> 00:34:23.140
Stop!

00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:25.600
Stop!

00:34:32.280 --> 00:34:33.800
You have to help me.

00:34:34.070 --> 00:34:35.960
Dean, I don't think
she knows she's dead.

00:34:39.460 --> 00:34:40.180
Please!

00:34:40.700 --> 00:34:41.270
Open up!

00:34:41.270 --> 00:34:41.690
Please!

00:34:41.690 --> 00:34:42.590
Okay. All right, all right.

00:34:42.590 --> 00:34:43.370
Just calm down.

00:34:43.370 --> 00:34:44.460
Tell us what happened.

00:34:44.530 --> 00:34:45.590
What are you gonna tell her?

00:34:46.510 --> 00:34:47.630
The truth.

00:34:48.210 --> 00:34:50.280
She's gonna take off running
in the other direction.

00:34:51.400 --> 00:34:53.280
Some spirits hold on too tight.

00:34:54.690 --> 00:34:55.900
Can't let go.

00:35:01.390 --> 00:35:02.400
And Greeley?

00:35:02.550 --> 00:35:07.560
Each year he punishes somebody
for his death... chasing them.

00:35:08.890 --> 00:35:10.410
Torturing them.

00:35:12.900 --> 00:35:16.950
And each year, that somebody is you.

00:35:17.210 --> 00:35:19.080
But I don't remember any of it.

00:35:19.240 --> 00:35:21.210
Because you couldn't
see the truth, Molly.

00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:29.100
So that's why he won't
let me off the highway.

00:35:31.380 --> 00:35:32.350
Because...

00:35:33.590 --> 00:35:35.120
I killed him.

00:35:37.510 --> 00:35:39.220
I killed us both.

00:35:46.440 --> 00:35:48.930
Why didn't you tell me
when you first saw me?

00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:51.260
Why wait until now?

00:35:51.670 --> 00:35:52.980
You wouldn't have believed us.

00:35:54.390 --> 00:35:55.870
And you needed me for bait.

00:35:58.590 --> 00:36:00.010
Well, we needed you.

00:36:03.560 --> 00:36:04.630
David.

00:36:04.890 --> 00:36:07.410
Molly, we brought you
here so you could move on.

00:36:08.380 --> 00:36:09.920
I have to tell him.

00:36:14.610 --> 00:36:15.560
That you love him?

00:36:16.320 --> 00:36:17.780
That you're sorry?

00:36:19.010 --> 00:36:21.010
Molly, he already knows that.

00:36:23.590 --> 00:36:26.130
Look, if you want to go in
there, we're not gonna stop you.

00:36:26.130 --> 00:36:28.460
Yeah, but you are gonna
freak him right out.

00:36:30.890 --> 00:36:32.020
For life.

00:36:42.730 --> 00:36:44.870
David's already said
his good byes, Molly.

00:36:45.490 --> 00:36:46.790
Now it's your turn.

00:36:47.560 --> 00:36:50.180
This is your unfinished business.

00:36:51.370 --> 00:36:53.090
What am I supposed to do?

00:36:55.650 --> 00:36:56.530
Just...

00:36:58.090 --> 00:36:58.960
Let go.

00:37:00.700 --> 00:37:01.700
Of David.

00:37:01.850 --> 00:37:03.260
Of everything.

00:37:04.520 --> 00:37:05.730
You do that...

00:37:06.960 --> 00:37:08.490
We think you'll move on.

00:37:09.880 --> 00:37:11.630
But you don't know where.

00:37:13.930 --> 00:37:15.160
No.

00:37:16.850 --> 00:37:18.750
Molly, you don't belong here.

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:21.980
Haven't you suffer edlong enough?

00:37:24.560 --> 00:37:25.810
It's time.

00:37:27.670 --> 00:37:29.240
It's time to go.

00:38:18.610 --> 00:38:20.190
I guess she wasn't so bad...

00:38:20.930 --> 00:38:22.040
For a ghost.

00:38:24.920 --> 00:38:26.810
You think she's really
going to a better place?

00:38:28.470 --> 00:38:29.630
I hope so.

00:38:31.760 --> 00:38:32.910
I guess we'll never know.

00:38:32.910 --> 00:38:35.070
Not until we take the
plunge ourselves, huh?

00:38:36.190 --> 00:38:37.450
Doesn't really matter, Dean.

00:38:39.720 --> 00:38:41.450
Hope's kind of the whole point.

00:38:44.820 --> 00:38:46.100
All right, Haley Joel.

00:38:47.740 --> 00:38:49.060
Let's hit the road.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
